  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-01-26T20:20:47.809Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There is no way to resize a texture in Udon currently. We can release (custom) render textures and that's about it. This is quite limiting and can hamper performance by forcing people to use the largest resolution needed when they could have otherwise reduced it as needed. If the issue with allowing resizing ((custom) render) textures is the possibility that they can be used to run the client out of memory, it would be useful to intercept the calls and cap the maximum resolution to something reasonable like 4k or 8k. This should have minimal performance overhead since people should not be resizing and reallocating their textures every frame. If that's the concern, it can be rate limited and just return false to the udon behaviour.",
